Planex antipattern_closure — why Closure is necessary
=========================================================
Shows: onClick/handler cannot express intent + goal + eval + lifecycle

[anti-pattern 1] Intent as a value, not a callback
  React: onClick={fn} — intent buried in callback, transient
  Planex: px_closure_last_intent() returns typed value, persistent
  After trigger: kind=REQUEST, payload=42 (serializable)
  PASS — intent is a value, can be serialized/replayed

[anti-pattern 2] Goal as a recorded field
  React: goal implicit in function name, lost on error
  Planex: goal is a field, used in error messages
  After dec to -1: feedback = "evaluation failed: goal "decrement counter" not achieved"
  PASS — goal recorded, used in error feedback

[anti-pattern 3] Auto-evaluation
  React: onClick fn returns void, no built-in success/failure
  Planex: eval fn returns bool, runtime auto-sets status
  After inc (eval succeeds): status=DONE, evaluated=true
  PASS — evaluation is automatic, status is auto-set

[anti-pattern 4] Async lifecycle (promise/declare/fail)
  React: 3 state vars (isLoading, error, data) for async
  Planex: closure has promise/declare/fail built-in
  After promise: status=RUNNING, feedback="Fetching user data..."
  After declare: status=DONE, feedback="User data loaded"
  After fail:    status=FAILED, feedback="Network error"
  PASS — async lifecycle is first-class

[anti-pattern 5] Speech-act typed Intent
  React: onClick is just a function, no semantic type
  Planex: 5 typed kinds (ASSERT/REQUEST/PROMISE/DECLARE/EXPRESS)
  All 5 kinds preserved: ASSERT, REQUEST, PROMISE, DECLARE, EXPRESS
  PASS — Intent has semantic type (Winograd/Flores speech acts)

=== Summary ===
Mainstream event (onClick/handler) requires FIVE patches:
  1. Manual logging layer for intent serialization
  2. Manual goal tracking for error messages
  3. try/catch + status state for evaluation
  4. 3 state vars for async lifecycle
  5. Convention-only semantic typing of intents

Planex Closure subsumes all five as first-class:
  1. px_closure_last_intent() returns typed value
  2. Goal is a field, used in auto-feedback
  3. eval fn returns bool, runtime auto-sets status
  4. promise/declare/fail built-in async lifecycle
  5. 5 typed Intent kinds (Winograd/Flores)

Closure is NECESSARY: onClick + patches is a strict subset.

=== Closure anti-pattern test complete ===
